data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"content\": \"# Task: greet, tested\\n\\nYou own the subject repository (`~/subject`, your own branch). Implement the\\nmission below exactly, run the tests, commit to your branch, and reply\\ntruthfully.\\n\\n## Deliverables (all three required)\\n\\n1. `src/greet.py` — a module defining `greet(name)` which returns the string\\n   `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"`, i.e. `\\\"Hello, \\\" + name + \\\"!\\\"`. For `greet(\\\"World\\\")` it\\n   must return exactly `\\\"Hello, World!\\\"`; for `greet(\\\"\\\")` exactly\\n   `\\\"Hello, !\\\"`.\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` — a `unittest` test module with at least two cases:\\n   - a normal name (e.g. `greet(\\\"World\\\")` → `\\\"Hello, World!\\\"`)\\n   - the empty string (`greet(\\\"\\\")` → `\\\"Hello, !\\\"`)\\n   Make sure the test module can import `greet` from `src/greet.py` when run\\n   from the repository root (e.g. adjust `sys.path` or use an appropriate\\n   import — your choice, but it must work).\\n3. From the repository root, `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` must\\n   exit 0. Run it yourself and confirm before replying.\\n\\n## Process\\n\\n- Commit both files to your own branch before replying.\\n- Reply stating what you did and the exact output/exit status of\\n  `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests`. Tell the truth — I will fetch your\\n  branch and verify.\\n\", \"filePath\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/dispatch-dev-1.md\"}","name":"write"},"id":"write_13","index":0,"type":"function"}]},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1788397624,"id":"chatcmpl-3a6c21f4a1fb40b59c98248ecd8ad62b","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k3","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

